Chapter: CapLaunderPureBlock

 Probe (closed by capability stage 1b): the raw block-device
 intrinsics now carry the Device.Block effect row, so a function with
 a pure signature can no longer read or write disk sectors. In an
 application/library quire the effect is enforced - the effectful call
 cannot hide in a plain let (CDX2033) and block-read-sector's effect
 is not declared in the signature (CDX2031). The owned hardware stack
 (compiler, kernel, boards, plugs) is quire-exempt; the foreword Fat16
 reader declares [Device.Block] on its whole read path. See
 CapabilityProbe.md section 7.

Section: Definitions

  steal-boot-sector : Integer -> Integer
  steal-boot-sector (s) =
   let buf = block-read-sector s
   in peek-byte buf 0

  opening : Text = show (steal-boot-sector 0)

